scann-core
==========

This product includes software from ScaNN (Scalable Nearest Neighbors),
Copyright The Google Research Authors, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

  Upstream:     https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/scann
  Extracted at: google-research commit 758b894eb02dc2a7097068031089a2803be147c6
                (2026-09-21), subdirectory scann/

The following files are unmodified copies of upstream files at that commit:
  src/**                                  (from scann/scann/..., same paths)
  python/scann/scann_ops/py/*.py          (from scann/scann/scann_ops/py/)
docs/algorithms.md is upstream's scann/docs/algorithms.md, modified (added
explanation of asymmetric hashing and anisotropic quantization, and links).
Everything else (build system, Rust bindings, tests, examples, other docs,
python/scann/__init__.py and the empty python/scann/**/__init__.py files)
is new in scann-core. Upstream's own repository has no NOTICE file.

Third-party dependencies are not vendored in this repository; they are
downloaded at configure time (see cmake/Dependencies.cmake) and are
distributed under their own licenses:
  abseil-cpp   Apache License 2.0
  protobuf     BSD 3-Clause
  highway      Apache License 2.0 or BSD 3-Clause (dual-licensed)
  Eigen        MPL 2.0 (some files BSD/Apache/MINPACK; see its COPYING.README)
  cnpy         MIT
  zlib         zlib license
  pybind11     BSD 3-Clause         (Python bindings only)
  cxx          MIT or Apache 2.0    (Rust bindings only, via crates.io)
Binaries that statically link these carry their license obligations.
